<title>HUNGARY: Hungary welfare minister offers resignation - TV.</title>
<headline>Hungary welfare minister offers resignation - TV.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian Welfare Minister Gyorgy Szabo has offered his resignation, Hungarian television reported on Wednesday evening.</p>
<p>Prime Minister Gyula Horn told the Socialist Party presidium about the offer at an afternoon meeting but said he had not yet decided whether to accept it, the TV said.</p>
<p>It said Szabo wanted to leave office for personal reasons.</p>
</text>
